WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.175
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will build a roster dispatch

00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:10.349
can use. An out-of-date roster leaves dispatchers guessing which station, team, or role

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:15.524
a member belongs to. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and

00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:18.310
a practical way to check the result.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.650
A volunteer department creates Station 1 and Station 2 groups, invites 24 members

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:30.389
and assigns Engineer and Firefighter roles. Dispatch, notifications, permissions and reports all start

00:00:30.389 --> 00:00:36.129
from who belongs to which group, so set this up first. The examples

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:41.868
in this series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not default

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:42.310
settings.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:48.538
Personnel. Member accounts, contact details and status. Invite members or add them directly,

00:00:48.538 --> 00:00:53.300
then check that each has a mobile number or email address.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.998
Manage Invites. Email invitations for new members to join the department. Send invitations

00:00:58.998 --> 00:01:02.920
and follow up on any that have not been accepted.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.976
Groups & Stations. Stations and groups that organize members and units. Create a

00:01:08.976 --> 00:01:14.431
station group for each station with its address, and organizational groups for teams,

00:01:14.431 --> 00:01:15.690
then add members.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:21.715
Personnel roles. Roles such as Firefighter, EMT or Officer. Create the roles you

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:25.470
dispatch or report on, and assign them to members.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.110
Add Person. Create a member account directly instead of sending an invitation. Have

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:36.149
your member list with email addresses or mobile numbers, and decide how stations

00:01:36.149 --> 00:01:37.700
or teams are grouped.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.183
New Group. Create a station or group. Have your member list with email

00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:47.690
addresses or mobile numbers, and decide how stations or teams are grouped.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.831
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Create Station 1

00:01:53.831 --> 00:01:59.372
and Station 2 with their addresses. Step 2. Invite sample members and assign

00:01:59.372 --> 00:02:04.914
their station groups. Step 3. Create Engineer and Officer roles and assign them

00:02:04.914 --> 00:02:05.340
deliberately.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:11.041
Now verify the result. Verify a sample member appears in the correct group

00:02:11.041 --> 00:02:16.142
and role. Check an accepted invitation and the member contact details. A common

00:02:16.142 --> 00:02:21.244
problem to watch for: An invitation is not an accepted membership. A role

00:02:21.244 --> 00:02:25.560
label is not proof of a current certification. Review both separately.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.291
Your practice task is simple. Invite one sample member, assign a station and

00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:36.422
role, and have that member sign in. Track unaccepted invitations. Record the result,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:41.553
who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the linked

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:44.710
feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

